      "math_academy_id": "e-2579",
      "problem": "Compute the measures of the shaded angles in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14173512/assets/6d39f6b553856204eb1958c84fb06dc2756edb4e44beee4c55550aad8d3592f4.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The two angles marked in the diagram are vertical. Since vertical angles are congruent, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-{15}^{∘} & =2x+{10}^{∘} \\\\ x-{15}^{∘} & ={10}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know $x=25^\\circ,$ we can substitute into one of the expressions to calculate the measure of the angles. Let's substitute into the expression $2x + 10^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n2x + 10^\\circ = 2 \\cdot 25^\\circ + 10^\\circ = 60^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, both angles have a measure of $60^\\circ.$",
